From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 023] panvk: shaderClipDistance/shaderCullDistance via FS discard
Generated-by: LLM

Purpose: Valhall has no clip/cull distance hardware. Lower on the GPU:
 - VS (preprocess): the compact ClipDistance/CullDistance arrays (separate,
   combined, or packed after the clip array at CLIP_DIST1) become temps;
   new vec4 outputs CLIP_DIST0/1 carry the clip distances (unused lanes
   +1.0) and CULL_DIST0/1 carry per-vertex "cull distance < 0" flags
   (1.0/0.0, unused lanes 0.0).
 - FS: discard when any interpolated clip distance < 0 or any interpolated
   cull flag >= 1 - 2^-16, i.e. every vertex of the primitive had that cull
   distance negative (barycentric weights are convex). Only slots the
   linked VS writes are read; unlinked FS reads all four, missing VS slots
   read as constant 0 (no discard). FS ClipDistance inputs get the
   interpolated value; FS CullDistance inputs read 0.
 - Varying link/attribute emission uses the slot section instead of
   location < VAR0, so generic slots below VAR0 (CLIP/CULL_DIST) get real
   buffer offsets.
 - Expose shaderClipDistance/shaderCullDistance, maxClipDistances =
   maxCullDistances = maxCombinedClipAndCullDistances = 8 on v10+.
Source/Reference: Mesa nir_lower_clip.c (nir_lower_clip_fs) at 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b;
 fork idea GunaCharanTeja 187662d (vec4 lowering, not taken: no cull semantics)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (0xb8a31030, PAN_ARCH 11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b
Dependencies: csf-v11/022
Validation test: tests/dxvk/vulkan/clip-cull/clip_cull.c (13/13 IDVS and
 PANVK_DEBUG=gpu_prerast)

